{:edb/db-before-t 2847 :edb/db-after-t 2848 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536160 50 #inst "2026-10-09T17:36:01.389Z" 13194139536160 true] [17592186064130 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386584 13194139536160 true] [17592186064130 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386605 13194139536160 true] [17592186064130 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386612 13194139536160 true] [17592186064131 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386591 13194139536160 true] [17592186064132 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386598 13194139536160 true] [17592186064132 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386619 13194139536160 true] [17592186064132 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386622 13194139536160 true] [17592186064162 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386629 13194139536160 true] [17592186064862 1017 #edb/ref 17592186063681 13194139536160 false] [17592186064862 1017 #edb/ref 17592186386636 13194139536160 true] [17592186064862 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139536160 true] [17592186064862 1100 "$\\int \\frac{2}{|x|\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" 13194139536160 true] [17592186064862 1100 "What is $∫\\frac{2}{\\mid x \\mid \\sqrt{4x^{2} - 1}}dx$?" 13194139536160 false] [17592186064862 1145 "Note that we can rewrite this integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{2\\,\\text{d}x}{|x|\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}-1}}=4\\int \\frac{\\text{d}x}{|2x|\\sqrt{(2x)^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nThis integral now resembles the basic one for $\\text{arcsec},$\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $2x.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=2x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2}{|x|\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =4\\int \\frac{1}{|2x|\\sqrt{(2x)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =2\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =2\\,\\text{arcsec}\\,u+C \\\\  & =2\\,\\text{arcsec}(2x)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536160 true] [17592186386584 1017 #edb/ref 17592186386585 13194139536160 true] [17592186386584 1089 "q-114022" 13194139536160 true] [17592186386584 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536160 true] [17592186386584 1100 "Calculate $\\int \\frac{5}{\\sqrt{1-25{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139536160 true] [17592186386584 1113 #uuid "06f9fcd3-7dc3-572e-aebd-f0b325ad80ff" 13194139536160 true] [17592186386584 1145 "This integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $25{x}^{2}=(5x)^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=5x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=5\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{5}{\\sqrt{1-25{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =5\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(5x)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\cdot (\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(5x)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536160 true] [17592186386585 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386586 13194139536160 true] [17592186386585 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386587 13194139536160 true] [17592186386585 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386588 13194139536160 true] [17592186386585 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386589 13194139536160 true] [17592186386585 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386590 13194139536160 true] [17592186386585 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536160 true] [17592186386585 1041 "selection" 13194139536160 true] [17592186386585 1104 #edb/ref 17592186386586 13194139536160 true] [17592186386585 1110 #uuid "3f936aa7-7cd5-5504-972d-8cf4ebdd6c21" 13194139536160 true] [17592186386586 10