\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{5}\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{100-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{3}{5}{\\int }_{0}^{5}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/10)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot 10\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =6{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}} \\\\  & =6\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u\\,{|}_{0}^{1/2} \\\\  & =6\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})-6\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(0) \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536160 true] [17592186386620 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386621 13194139536160 true] [17592186386620 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139536160 true] [17592186386620 1041 "field-1" 13194139536160 true] [17592186386620 1104 #edb/ref 17592186386621 13194139536160 true] [17592186386620 1110 #uuid "99344a88-225a-56e8-a799-6537b9be6eff" 13194139536160 true] [17592186386621 1034 "\\pi" 13194139536160 true] [17592186386621 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536160 true] [17592186386621 1111 #uuid "4e811957-3537-5ea5-9cc8-a914c4846733" 13194139536160 true] [17592186386622 1017 #edb/ref 17592186386623 13194139536160 true] [17592186386622 1089 "q-49538" 13194139536160 true] [17592186386622 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536160 true] [17592186386622 1100 "What is the value of ${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+4{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,?$" 13194139536160 true] [17592186386622 1113 #uuid "b78003dc-845c-57d9-8ac3-a4f2236098d1" 13194139536160 true] [17592186386622 1145 "This integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $4{x}^{2}=(2x)^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=2x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$